<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  TOMBSTONE. This is the launchd job description for SentryFanDaemon, the
  root helper older builds of Sentry could install to write SMC fan keys.
  Sentry does not set fan speeds any more: the daemon target, its binary,
  and every line of code that could write a fan key are gone, and fan RPM
  is now something the app only reads and displays.

  THIS FILE STILL SHIPS, ON PURPOSE, AND IT IS THE ONLY REASON AN ALREADY-
  INSTALLED DAEMON CAN BE REMOVED. Users who pressed Install in the old
  Settings ▸ Fans pane have this job registered on their Mac right now.
  `Sentry/App/FanDaemonUninstaller.swift` unregisters it on launch through
  `SMAppService.daemon(plistName:)`, which resolves a service by looking
  this exact file up by basename inside
  Sentry.app/Contents/Library/LaunchDaemons/. Delete the file and every Mac
  reports `.notFound`, the uninstaller can no longer distinguish "never
  installed" from "installed and now invisible", and a root process with no
  owner becomes permanent. Deleting the plist before unregistering is
  exactly how an orphaned daemon is created.

  NOTHING BELOW IS LIVE. `BundleProgram` names a binary this app no longer
  contains. A job description installs nothing by itself — it does nothing
  at all until something registers it, and nothing in this build registers
  anything. The keys are left byte-for-byte as they shipped because they
  describe a job already recorded on other people's machines; changing them
  would describe a different job than the one that needs removing.

  DELETE THIS FILE only together with `FanDaemonUninstaller`, its call in
  `AppDelegate`, and the copy phase in project.yml — once no install in the
  field can still predate the fan-control removal. See the uninstaller's
  doc comment.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>Label</key>
	<string>dev.malekswilam.sentry.fandaemon</string>

	<!-- Relative to Sentry.app. The Sentry target's Copy Files phase puts
	     the built tool at Contents/MacOS/SentryFanDaemon; see project.yml. -->
	<key>BundleProgram</key>
	<string>Contents/MacOS/SentryFanDaemon</string>

	<!-- Must match FanDaemonNaming.machService exactly — the app dials this
	     string via NSXPCConnection(machServiceName:options:.privileged). -->
	<key>MachServices</key>
	<dict>
		<key>dev.malekswilam.sentry.fandaemon</key>
		<true/>
	</dict>

	<!-- What macOS shows the user in System Settings ▸ General ▸ Login
	     Items & Extensions. Without it the entry is an unexplained
	     background item; with it, it is attributed to Sentry, which is the
	     only honest presentation of a root process this app installed. It
	     is also the entry the user toggles off to disable the helper
	     without deleting anything. -->
	<key>AssociatedBundleIdentifiers</key>
	<array>
		<string>dev.malekswilam.sentry</string>
	</array>

	<!-- Adaptive: the daemon spends essentially all its time asleep on a
	     dispatch queue, but a fan write should not be scheduled behind a
	     background maintenance task. -->
	<key>ProcessType</key>
	<string>Adaptive</string>
</dict>
</plist>
